IMPORT prelude

-- Private Education Act 2009 (Singapore) -- what counts as "private education" (the Schedule), who the Act does not touch
-- (s 45), the duty to register and the bar on suing for fees (s 7), two grounds for refusing registration (s 10(1)(a), (c)),
-- the notice owed to students when an institution closes (s 14(1)(b)), the Agency's power to direct course money refunds
-- (s 33), misleading advertisements (s 19), the administrative penalty cap (s 21), and the penalty and composition ceilings
-- (ss 34, 40).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021), informal consolidation "version in force
-- from 1/7/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PEA2009.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 17 of 2026
-- wef 01/07/2026 (the Agency is now the Skills and Workforce Development Agency; a definition of "private education
-- institution for adult learners" is added).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone in Singapore who pays a private school, diploma provider,
-- international school or full-time exam-preparation course is dealing with an institution this Act regulates, and the
-- refund and closure-notice rules are what a student meets when things go wrong. SCOPED to those provisions. Not encoded:
-- the Agency and Committee (Part 2), registration procedure (ss 8, 9), the rest of the refusal and suspension grounds
-- (ss 10, 11, beyond the form-of-entity and teachers grounds, the 6-month suspension cap and the 14-day wait), names
-- (ss 12, 13), managers' other duties (s 14(1)(a), (c)-(f), (2)), course permission (s 16) beyond its effect on s 7(10),
-- teachers (ss 17, 18), accreditation schemes (ss 22, 23), appeals (Part 5), inspection (ss 29-32), requisitions,
-- registers and dispute resolution schemes (ss 35-37), service, regulations and transitional provisions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Private Education Act 2009 -- courses and providers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `The Schedule -- what is private education`

-- Schedule para 1: "full-time" means education "of a duration of at least one month and that is conducted for 5 days of a
-- week for at least 3 hours each day"; "post-secondary education" means education "normally for a person who is 16 years of
-- age or above"; "primary or secondary education" means education "normally for a child who is above 6 years of age and
-- below 18 years of age".
-- Para 2: private education is any of (a) "education leading to the award of a diploma or degree"; (b) "full-time
-- post-secondary education leading to the award of a certificate"; (c) "full-time primary or secondary education wholly or
-- substantially in accordance with a foreign or international curriculum"; (d) "full-time special education for students
-- with physical or intellectual disabilities"; (e) full-time exam preparation for an examination that (i) leads to a
-- qualification awarded by someone else or (ii) entitles students to be admitted to an education institution -- "whether
-- provided wholly or in part electronically, through correspondence or in any other manner".
-- Para 3: it does NOT include (a) an apprenticeship or (b) "any education provided by any employer exclusively for the
-- employer's employees".
--
-- "5 days of a week" is read as AT LEAST 5 days (an inference; the text does not say "at least" for days).
DECLARE Course HAS
    `months long` IS A NUMBER
    `days a week` IS A NUMBER
    `hours a day` IS A NUMBER
    `leads to a diploma or degree` IS A BOOLEAN
    `leads to a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is post-secondary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is primary or secondary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `follows a foreign or international curriculum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is special education for students with disabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prepares for an outside qualification or an admission exam` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is given by an employer only to its own employees` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the course` IS A Course
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the course is full-time` IF
        `the course`'s `months long` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the course`'s `days a week` AT LEAST 5
    AND `the course`'s `hours a day` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `the course` IS A Course
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the course is private education` IF
        (NOT `the course`'s `is an apprenticeship`)
    AND (NOT `the course`'s `is given by an employer only to its own employees`)
    AND (    `the course`'s `leads to a diploma or degree`
         OR  (`the course is full-time` `the course` AND `the course`'s `is post-secondary` AND `the course`'s `leads to a certificate`)
         OR  (`the course is full-time` `the course` AND `the course`'s `is primary or secondary` AND `the course`'s `follows a foreign or international curriculum`)
         OR  (`the course is full-time` `the course` AND `the course`'s `is special education for students with disabilities`)
         OR  (`the course is full-time` `the course` AND `the course`'s `prepares for an outside qualification or an admission exam`))

§§ `45 -- providers the Act does not apply to`

-- s 45(1): the Act "does not apply to" (a) the Government and Government schools; (b) ITE; (c) the five named Polytechnics;
-- (d) other public bodies with a public function; (e) government-aided schools (unless notified); (f) subvented special
-- education schools; (g) institutions "providing education in accordance with religious beliefs and principles and no other
-- education"; (h) schools under the School Boards (Incorporation) Act; (i) NTU, NUS, SMU, SUTD, SIT, SUSS and others whose
-- university function is determined by written law; (j) places of safety and similar. s 45(2): nor to licensed early
-- childhood development centres.
DECLARE Provider IS ONE OF
    `a private company`
    `a registered society`
    `a sole proprietor`
    `a partnership`
    `a Government school`
    `ITE`
    `a polytechnic`
    `an autonomous university`
    `a purely religious school`
    `a licensed childcare or preschool centre`
    `a subvented special education school`

GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the provider` IF
    CONSIDER `the provider`
    WHEN `a private company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered society` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sole proprietor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a partnership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- registration, and suing for fees`

-- s 7(1): a person in Singapore "must not" offer to provide or provide private education, or award a degree, diploma or
-- certificate in respect of it, "unless the person is a registered private education institution"; (2) offence; (3)
-- "knowingly assists" an unregistered institution is an offence; (6) the Agency may direct an unregistered institution to
-- refund "the whole of the course money", despite any contract (7).
-- s 7(10): "no person is entitled to recover in any court any charge, course money or remuneration for any private education
-- provided in Singapore unless" the provider is registered AND provided it "in accordance with the permission of the Agency
-- under section 16 required for the course".
GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider, `the course` IS A Course
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registration is required` IF
    `the Act applies to the provider` `the provider` AND `the course is private education` `the course`

GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider, `the course` IS A Course, `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offering the course is an offence` IF
    `registration is required` `the provider` `the course` AND (NOT `is registered`)

GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider, `the course` IS A Course, `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `has course permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fees can be sued for` IF
        (NOT `registration is required` `the provider` `the course`)
    OR  (`is registered` AND `has course permission`)

§§ `10(1)(a), (c) -- two grounds for refusing registration`

-- s 10(1): the Agency "may refuse" if (a) "the private education institution is not a company or a registered society"; ...
-- (c) "all or more than half of the total number of teachers ... do not possess the minimum qualifications or experience" or
-- are otherwise not fit and proper. s 11(1)(a), (c) repeat these as grounds to suspend or cancel. Exactly half is not enough.
GIVEN `the provider` IS A Provider
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form of the institution is a ground for refusal` IF
    CONSIDER `the provider`
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a registered society` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `unqualified teachers` IS A NUMBER, `all teachers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the teaching staff is a ground for refusal` IF
        `all teachers` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (    `unqualified teachers` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `all teachers`
         OR  `unqualified teachers` EQUALS `all teachers`)

§§ `11(1), (5) -- suspension`

-- s 11(1): the Agency may "suspend (for a period not exceeding 6 months) or cancel" a registration. (5): subject to s 26,
-- the decision "must not take effect until the expiry of 14 days after the Agency has served the notice of the decision".
-- Reading "until the expiry of 14 days" as "only after day 14" is an inference about counting.
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within the cap` IF
    `months` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `days since notice was served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension may already take effect` IF
    `days since notice was served` GREATER THAN 14

§§ `14(1)(b) -- telling students the institution is closing`

-- s 14(1)(b): a manager must ensure the Agency and "each student and intending student" are told in writing of the cessation
-- and of the arrangements for a place "in another registered private education institution to complete the same or similar
-- course": (i) where the cessation is because registration was not renewed, or was suspended, cancelled or cut short -- "at
-- least 14 days before the cessation" (or another period the Agency allows); (ii) "for any other reason -- at least 30 days
-- before the cessation". (3): failure without reasonable excuse is an offence.
--
-- The institution that closes on its own gets the LONGER notice period.
DECLARE Closure IS ONE OF
    `registration not renewed`
    `registration suspended`
    `registration cancelled`
    `the owners decide to close`
    `the institution runs out of money`

GIVEN `the closure` IS A Closure
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum days of notice to students` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the closure`
    WHEN `registration not renewed` THEN 14
    WHEN `registration suspended` THEN 14
    WHEN `registration cancelled` THEN 14
    OTHERWISE 30

GIVEN `the closure` IS A Closure, `days of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the students had enough notice` IF
    `days of notice given` AT LEAST `the minimum days of notice to students` `the closure`

§§ `33 -- course money refunds`

-- s 33(1): applies to a student or intending student if (a) "the course does not start on the agreed starting day"; (b) "the
-- course ceases to be provided at any time after it starts but before it is completed"; or (c) it is not provided in full
-- because of a refusal to renew, or a suspension, cancellation or reduction of registration -- "and the student or intending
-- student has not withdrawn from the private education institution before the default day".
-- (2): the Agency "may" direct a refund of "the whole or such part as the Agency deems equitable" of the course money, and/or
-- a place elsewhere. (3): this applies "despite anything contained in the agreement or contract", and the student may recover
-- the directed amount "as a civil debt". (4): the institution "is relieved of its liability to make a refund if the student
-- ... accepts the offer ... to complete the same or a similar course at the private education institution's expense".
--
-- s 33 is a power of the Agency, not a student's automatic right: dissatisfaction or a change of mind is not a trigger.
DECLARE Trouble IS ONE OF
    `the course did not start on the agreed day`
    `the course stopped part-way`
    `the course was cut short by regulatory action`
    `the student changed their mind`
    `the student was unhappy with the teaching`

GIVEN `the trouble` IS A Trouble, `withdrew before the default day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may direct a refund` IF
        (NOT `withdrew before the default day`)
    AND CONSIDER `the trouble`
        WHEN `the student changed their mind` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `the student was unhappy with the teaching` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `a refund was directed` IS A BOOLEAN, `accepted a place elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN, `the place is at the institution's expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the student can sue for the refund` IF
        `a refund was directed`
    AND (NOT (`accepted a place elsewhere` AND `the place is at the institution's expense`))

§§ `19 -- misleading advertisements`

-- s 19(1): a person "must not knowingly or recklessly" issue or publish an advertisement relating to a private education
-- institution "which is false or misleading in a material particular". (2)(b): it is "presumed, unless the contrary is
-- proved", to be false or misleading if it (i) falsely describes the institution; (ii) contains false or misleading
-- information about it or any course; or (iii) lacks prescribed information. (3): $5,000 or 6 months or both.
GIVEN `falsely describes the institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `contains false course information` IS A BOOLEAN, `omits prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN, `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advertisement is taken to be misleading` IF
        (`falsely describes the institution` OR `contains false course information` OR `omits prescribed information`)
    AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

GIVEN `misleading` IS A BOOLEAN, `knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `publishing it is an offence` IF
    `misleading` AND `knowingly or recklessly`

§§ `21, 34, 40 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 21(1)(c): for a breach of a registration condition, or of s 12(1) or 17(1), the Agency may impose "a financial penalty of
-- any amount, not exceeding $5,000". s 37(3)(a) has the same cap for dispute resolution breaches.
-- s 34(1): false statements in applications, obstructing inspectors and similar: "$5,000 or ... 6 months or ... both".
-- s 34(2): any offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided": "$10,000 or ... 12 months or ... both" and, for a
-- continuing offence, "a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day" after conviction.
-- s 40(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the
-- amount of the maximum fine" or (b) "$5,000".
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the administrative penalty is within the cap` IF
    `amount` AT MOST 5000

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `running an unregistered institution`
    `knowingly helping an unregistered institution`
    `ignoring a refund direction`
    `a manager failing to give closure notice`
    `publishing a misleading advertisement`
    `lying in a registration application`
    `obstructing an inspector`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence has its own penalty` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `publishing a misleading advertisement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `lying in a registration application` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence has its own penalty` `the offence` THEN 5000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the offence has its own penalty` `the offence` THEN 6 ELSE 12

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence has its own penalty` `the offence`
    THEN `the maximum fine` `the offence`
    ELSE `the maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
